WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
How do you turn a community meeting into useful research?

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Start with the decision, not the event.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Describe what people can influence, what is already fixed,
and who will make the final choice.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.000
More meetings do not automatically mean more influence.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Next, ask whose experience could be missing.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
A convenient meeting time for your team may not work
for the people you need to hear from.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:33.000
For example, an organization reviewing a service could
combine a small discussion with individual interviews.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
That is an illustrative planning example,
not a PRC project result.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:46.000
Explain how the findings will be considered, and report back
on what changed and what could not change.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:51.000
Keep participation separate from a promise to adopt every idea.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:58.000
PRC Impact helps organizations connect community listening
with research and practical recommendations.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:09.000
